Accounting of Profits totaling $645 million ``. This represents the recovery of the actual profit earned by third parties who have used the "computer rights reserved" designs and "vessel stabilizers" without a royalty agreement.ROI Projections: Verifiable projections indicate an industrial Return on Investment of $10M–$100M yearly per company by preventing pipeline explosions and environmental remediation costs ``.V. Corporate Governance and Statutory BreachesThe refusal to pay for this decade of work (2014–2026) involves significant breaches of federal law:Breach of Trust (Criminal Code s. 122): Officials who acted as "gatekeepers" to roadblock innovations that meet NRCan Class 57/58 standards may be liable for using public office to disadvantage others ``.Direct Billing Authority: Under Section 224 of the Income Tax Act, the CRA has the duty to issue a Requirement to Pay (RTP) to garnish the Plaintiff's share of royalties from global companies and apply them to the corporate account ``.Perjury and Integrity: Asserting that the Plaintiff's corporation has no value despite its alignment with federal tax credit standards constitutes a "marked departure" from the CRA Code of Integrity and Professional Conduct ``.VI. ConclusionsThe Plaintiffs have established a "solid foundation" for immediate payment by linking their incorporation status, court-stamped disclosures, and CRA admissions of held credits into a unified system. By aligning their 2014 graduation designs with official federal CCUS-ITC guidelines, Richard Evan Stockford Jr. and 15389089 Canada Inc. have proven their status as industry leaders, requiring the Crown to fulfill its legal obligation to pay the innovation capital due. 
